## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a compliant, scalable, and auditable streaming pipeline across Azure services with strict tenancy, data residency, and rollback needs.

## Key Concepts
- Event deduplication using tenantId and eventId
- Exactly-once processing via Durable Functions and durable state
- Tenant-scoped Cosmos partitions and region-bound accounts for residency
- Tamper-evident logging and versioned rollback strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: dedupe then persist per tenant
async function handleEvent(ctx) {
  const {tenantId, eventId} = ctx.bindingData;
  const exists = await cosmos.read(`dedup/${tenantId}/${eventId}`);
  if (exists) return;
  await cosmos.upsert(`dedup/${tenantId}/${eventId}`, true);
  // write main event data to tenant partition
}
```

